  "result": "Perfect! All 76 tests pass. I've added invoice rendering functionality:\n\n**New module: src/render.js**\n\n**`renderInvoiceText(invoice)`** \u2014 Renders an invoice as plain text for customers:\n- First line: Invoice number (or \"DRAFT\" if it has none)\n- Second line: Customer's name (looked up from customers module, falls back to customerId if not found)\n- Empty line\n- One line per invoice item showing: `<qty>x <name> @ <unit price> = <line total>`\n- Empty line\n- Last line: `Total: <total amount>`\n\n**Key features:**\n- All monetary amounts use `formatEuros()` for consistent customer-facing formatting\n- Handles quantity display (singular \"1x\" vs plural \"2x\")\n- Works with multiple line items and different VAT rates\n- Gracefully handles customer lookup failures\n\n**Test coverage:**\n\nAdded 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Draft (DRAFT) vs issued invoices (with number)\n- Customer name lookup and fallback to customerId\n- Single and multiple line items\n- Quantity formatting\n- Proper use of formatEuros for all amounts\n- Large amounts and thousands separators\n- VAT-exempt items\n- Output structure (multiline string)\n\nAll 76 tests pass \u2705",
